00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:45.470
And just a quick recap
of all the things.

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:49.130
It was launched in
I/O in May of 2018.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:53.330
Originally a Python runtime
with a Memcache API.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:57.350
Introduced Java
runtime in April 2009.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:02.300
And App Engine moved
out of preview in 2011.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:07.850
We introduced a Go runtime in
2012, a PHP runtime in 2013.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.550
Java 8, last year in
June, and most recently

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.920
in I/O, with Steren
over here, we

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.680
introduced the
world to Node.js.8

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:20.650
on App Engine standard on our
new second generation runtime.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:23.440
So our new second
generation runtime

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.560
is open source,
idiomatic experience.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.450
You write code the
same way for App Engine

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:31.930
that you would to just run
on any version of the runtime

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:32.680
you're writing.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:35.290
If you know how to write Python
to run it on your computer,

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:38.740
you know how to write Python
to run it on App Engine.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.270
The new second
generation runtime

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:43.900
can use any extension,
or binary, or framework.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.174
If you're writing Node,
pretty much any Node module

00:02:46.174 --> 00:02:47.590
that you want to
use, you can use.

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:50.914
Any Java library
or Python library,

00:02:50.914 --> 00:02:53.080
the things that are running
on the second generation

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:53.860
can run them.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:56.110
And this is a big difference
from the first generation

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:56.680
runtime.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:00.460
And as I mentioned, Node
8, we announced at I/O.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:03.160
But today, we wanted to let you
know about two new runtimes,

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.430
which are Python 3.7
and PHP 7.2, which

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:09.942
you can use on App Engine
today, which is really exciting.

00:03:09.942 --> 00:03:11.806
